    "intake_lift_source": "[AS] shape: the A25A's digitised SAE 2019-01-0249 Fig. 11 curves, x stretched by 1.084949 (intake) / 1.087370 (exhaust) so the 1 mm crossings land on IVO -34.2 / IVC 175.0 and EVO 500.0 / EVC 709.2 deg at zero cam phase ([AS] The 2.7 L workbooks carry no overlap, stroke-length or Atkinson column, and its 'Intake Cam Phaser Retard' (+15..+53 deg at high load) has an unknown zero (the 1.6 L workbook's retard is negative, i.e. advance, at its high-load rows). The zero-phase IVC0 is therefore PLACED so that the 2000 rpm envelope row closes at ~225 deg (IVC0 175 + 53 deg retard; the other engines' high-load IVC is 200-235 deg), EVO0 500 deg (40 BBDC, the Mazda fixture's rule), 1 mm durations 209.2 deg each (the Ford 1.6 L's [D] value) -> ov0 +23.4 deg by the duration identity. Only the measured cam DELTAS are [M]; absolute valve events of this engine are assumed. Phase B should treat the 2.7 L IVC as uncertain by ~+-30 deg.); lift x 0.948571 (bore ratio, L/D held).",
    "runner_length_mm": 930.6907,
    "runner_length_mm_source": "[AS] Tier 3 quarter-wave rule (the A25A's): 4L/a = the intake-open time (262.56 deg span) at 4000 rpm (tuning speed [AS], the Mazda 2.0 fixture's 4000), a = 340.29 m/s.",
